WEBVTT

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.600
<i>When I was a young child, 
I went on the town camping trip</i>

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.780
<i>and met a certain boy.</i>

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.660
Hey!

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.260
What are you doing out here?

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.470
What am I doing?

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.740
Letting my anger cool off.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.240
The lights from the campsite are interfering.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.200
That's Jupiter.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.230
Which one?

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.280
Here.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:00:59.710
Thanks.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.380
Look, over there.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.860
Oh! The dot!

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.710
Dot...

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.870
Well, yeah.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.400
You can't see it with binoculars,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.440
but Jupiter has stripes 
and thin rings around it.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.590
It also has about 70 moons.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.480
You know a lot!

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.180
Hey, what's your name?

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.100
Ao.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.620
I'm Mira!

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.600
The variable star!

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.880
Terrible start?

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.810
No, not that.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:35.530
<b>In the evening, the long-period variable star Mira of the Cetus 
constellation in the southwest sky will reach peak magnitude.</b>

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:31.810
The variable star Mira.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.530
It's a star in the Cetus constellation that's 
unusual because its brightness varies.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.110
Wow! I have the same name as a star?

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.440
What about you, Ao?

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.210
Is there a star with your name?

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.910
There's no star with a weird name like that.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.810
It's not weird! It's cool!

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:48.460
Huh?

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.880
Besides, if there isn't one, 
why not name one after you?

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.360
Name one?

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.670
An asteroid, maybe...

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.130
If I discover one of those, 
I should be able to name it.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.140
Let's find one, then!

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.190
Huh?

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.390
Let's discover the star Ao!

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.860
<i>That was the last time I saw that boy...</i>

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.030
<i>And now I'm in high school.</i>

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.990
I'm very happy to be enjoying life together 
with you all here at the same school.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.450
As we each work toward our goals and dreams,

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.710
let us study diligently together.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.170
<i>Starting today, I'm a high schooler!</i>

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.920
<i>And the one thing I wanted to do 
after starting high school is...</i>

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.880
<b>Club Listings</b>

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.880
...gone!

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.510
<b>Congratulations on Starting School</b>

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.510
Huh? What's wrong, Mira?

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.840
Suzu-chan!

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.140
The astronomy club that was 
here until last year is gone!

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.860
I was totally set on joining 
it in high school! Why?!

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.240
Yeah, about that...

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.040
Oh, uh...

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.320
Endou-sensei.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.810
Starting this year, the astronomy 
club and the geology club have been

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.280
merged into the earth sciences club.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.560
Earth sciences club?

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.700
I can't believe the clubs were merged.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.580
Maybe they weren't very popular?

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.330
That's not true!

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.080
<b>Astronomy Club
 This Way</b>

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.520
At last year's cultural festival...

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.290
She's cute!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.760
Earth Sciences

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.760
Sexy 
Planetarium

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.760
Come to our sexy planetarium!

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.040
...it was a huge hit!

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.090
Maybe that's the reason?

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:26.270
Setting aside their chastisement 
for the cultural festival...

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.720
They did get chastised for it?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.860
They lost members, and there were 
other issues on the school's end.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.270
So it was merged with the geology club 
to form the earth sciences club.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:43.490
Looking up at the sky and looking down at 
the ground are completely different, though.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:45.360
You think so?

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.240
They're both the same when you're 
looking from space, aren't they?

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:51.800
Wow! You've got a galactic perspective!

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:53.580
Stop it. That's embarrassing.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:00.280
Um, isn't the club room a bit far?

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:04.050
Its building is way out 
at the far end of campus.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.020
Isn't this building kind of old?

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:15.520
Th-There are still a few holes that 
let drafts in, but we fixed the leaks.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.480
Hey, I've brought some 
girls here to observe you.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.360
<b>Earth</b>

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.360
<b>Man</b>

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.360
<b>Heaven</b>

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.600
Heaven, Earth, man?

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.270
Are we at war?

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:29.810
I don't think so.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:32.160
Sorry.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.870
We haven't really adjusted to the merger yet.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:39.840
<b>Heaven</b>

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.400
I'm the club president, Morino.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.840
I used to be in the astronomy club.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.140
I'm the vice president, Sakurai.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.340
I used to be in the geology club.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:46.680
So, which are you?

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:46.680
<b>Earth</b>

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.020
Which?

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:53.270
Geology or astronomy!
Which were you hoping for?

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.930
If you're here for the geology club,

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:59.040
you get this power stone set that boosts 
your luck! For new members only!

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.150
Vice President! You'll make 
us lose more members!

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:04.260
I'm sorry.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.990
Our vice president's very concerned 
about our membership ratio.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:11.120
Oh, I'm Inose, a second-year on the geology side.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.380
I'm Manaka, a first-year. 
I was hoping for the astronomy club.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:19.250
There are other new students here!
 I was hoping for the astronomy club, too!

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.980
You like stars?

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:22.590
I do!

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.550
And there's something I want to do!

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.010
I want to discover an asteroid!

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.390
Oh? That's an awfully big goal.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.100
Is that hard to do?

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:39.060
There is a record of a high schooler 
discovering one in the past, but...

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.770
It's practically impossible 
for a tiny club like ours.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:45.280
You're being too harsh, Vice President!

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:46.760
Yes...

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.160
But I made a promise.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.620
With a boy, a long time ago.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:52.510
What?!

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.550
I never heard about this, Mira!

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:58.360
Well, if I told you about it, 
you'd dig into who he was, right?

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.290
Yes! I'd string him up! Gimme his name!

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:01.860
Ao.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:07.860
We promised to discover an 
asteroid together and name it Ao.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.510
I never saw him again after that, though.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:15.140
Oh, dear. Could that possibly be...

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.730
I think it might...

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.810
You're bright red, Manaka.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:21.890
Manaka Ao.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:25.110
What?!

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.950
Ao? <i>The</i> Ao? You're a girl?!

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:34.080
My name's kind of boyish, 
and my hair was short...

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:37.380
Y-Y-You remember me?!

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.510
Of course!

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:42.310
I've wanted to discover an 
asteroid ever since that day.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.710
And this...

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.250
A whale mascot?

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:49.510
So you wouldn't forget my name?

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.340
Well, well.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:56.470
Sounds like things are getting fun.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:01.830
<i>The boy I met that day was actually a girl.</i>

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:37.990
01. Their Promise

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:42.500
<i>Good evening!</i>

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.390
<i>Today was a big surprise!</i>

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:47.740
<i>I never imagined you'd be in the 
same high school club as me!</i>

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:50.300
<i>I'm so happy we're reunited!</i>

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.720
<i>I'm really sorry I mistook you for a boy.</i>

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.180
<i>It's good to see you again!</i>

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.510
M-Mom!

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.160
I'm borrowing a book!

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.020
Huh?

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.620
<i>I wonder if she's planning 
to get a part-time job...</i>

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:16.910
Mira.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.410
What's with that look?

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:24.330
Hey, you were finally reunited with the 
sweetheart you've longed for all these years.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.980
Smile, smile.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.620
Sweetheart?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.330
You're having fun with 
this for once, Suzu-chan.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:35.500
You always do mean things to the 
people who try to get close to me.

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:39.430
Well, that's because Manaka-san's 
a girl, and she's cute.

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:42.900
If it's a girl, then I'm totally okay with it.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:43.850
What?

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.080
So, what's up?

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:47.560
This...

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.020
Hmm, that's pretty formal.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:55.080
She used to be way more frank.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.300
I wonder if she doesn't like me now...

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.240
The only thing I can say is...

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:02.940
You sent too many texts.

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:04.240
Huh?! I did?!

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:07.500
If you're that worried, 
go talk to her in person.

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:12.250
The best thing about you is that you take 
action without overthinking things.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:14.630
Yeah.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.780
Excuse me!

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.260
At least think a little, though!

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:19.520
Oh, she's there!

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:22.420
Ao! Want to eat lunch together?

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:27.430
Sorry. Mira's rushing into things.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:28.190
It's fine.

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:32.490
Ao, I'm sorry I sent you 
all those texts last night!

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:33.170
Huh?

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:34.920
I was bothering you, wasn't I?

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.690
I'll cut back a little next time.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:40.310
N-No, it wasn't a bother at all.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:42.860
Really? Oh, good!

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:48.410
I'm sorry, too, for not being 
able to send cute replies.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.310
<i>That's so cute!</i>

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.120
Don't mind her.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.490
Suzu-chan's always been that way.

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:56.880
S-Sure.

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:01.770
You're really different from 
when you were younger.

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:05.440
I thought you were pretty chatty 
back during the camping trip.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.880
Now you have this mature, 
cool beauty thing going on.

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.230
Hey, Mira!

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.020
I'll go wash it real quick!

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:20.110
She should learn from your composure.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.450
I'm not composed at all, though.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:28.020
I keep panicking at my lack of words.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.160
I'm so nervous about 
messing up in front of Mira.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:35.250
Messing up what?

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:40.970
I really embarrassed myself in the 
past by saying the wrong thing...

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.010
So hot...

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.940
It's so wet today.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.700
Ao-chan, don't you mean humid?

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.850
Ao-chan said something dirty!

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:56.060
Dirty Ao-chan!

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.020
Ever since then, I've had trouble speaking.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.780
<i>That changed her personality?!</i>

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:05.740
I'm sure you know far 
more words than Mira does.

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:09.660
I'm her childhood friend, so I know.

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:13.510
You'll be fine.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:17.100
You're going to discover an 
asteroid together, right?

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:18.000
Yeah...

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:23.000
If you share the same dream, 
I'm sure you'll get along in no time.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:27.850
Suzu-chan, what do I do about this?

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:28.890
Mira!

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:32.830
Jeez, it would have come out if you'd 
just patted it with a handkerchief!

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.310
But...

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:44.150
<i>I know what Suzu-san said, 
but I'm still nervous.</i>

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:48.530
<i>You're really different from 
when you were younger.</i>

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:51.790
<i>My hair and body have grown, 
and I speak less,</i>

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:54.350
<i>so I imagine I do seem different now.</i>

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:57.910
<i>But my feelings...</i>

00:12:56.020 --> 00:13:00.210
Mira

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:02.940
<i>Hello?</i>

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:05.960
Um, hello... This is—

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:07.080
<i>Ow!</i>

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:08.480
Huh? Mira?!

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.760
<i>Sorry about that!</i>

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.740
<i>I just found something cool!</i>

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:15.100
H-Huh? That was from something good?

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.590
Ao, can you see outside right now?

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.060
To the west! The western sky!

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:27.470
<i>That's Mercury, right?</i>

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:27.910
Yeah.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.900
I got it right!

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:33.410
I've been studying a lot thanks to you, Ao!

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:36.060
<i>Ao?</i>

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:38.880
I'm fine. It's nothing.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.320
<i>I'm sorry for calling out of the blue.</i>

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:44.640
<i>I didn't really have anything to talk about.</i>

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:47.590
Oh, that's totally fine. Let's chat.

00:13:48.630 --> 00:13:50.050
<i>Chat?</i>

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.230
Hey, so, is Venus visible right now?

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:55.770
<i>Oh, uh...</i>

00:13:56.340 --> 00:14:00.230
I think you can see it shining really 
brightly in the mornings right now.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:03.500
It's probably around magnitude -4.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:06.700
Yeah, uh-huh.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.160
Morning.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:10.860
Morning!

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.990
Hmm? You seem happy.

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:17.510
Yeah! I chatted with Ao a lot last night!

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:19.460
Oh? Good for you.

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:22.340
Which means...

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:28.510
Suzu-chan, Ao's not a cool beauty at all.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.520
She's super cute!

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:36.690
Homeroom's starting.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.000
<b>First Earth Sciences Club Meeting!</b>

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:45.040
Time for the first...

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.240
...earth sciences club meeting!

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.990
So, what are we doing?

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.700
Earth Sciences Club 
Activity Schedule

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:56.280
We haven't clearly defined what 
our club activities are yet.

00:14:56.280 --> 00:15:00.790
So if there's anything you think we should 
do or have, we'll take suggestions.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.200
I want this!

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.000
<b>30m Aperture Telescope Project</b>

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.000
<b>The project to build 
the world's largest telescope
 with the aid of five 
different nations has begun</b>

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.000
Rejected!

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:06.500
Huh? But you just said to say what we wanted.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:10.340
You need to think of things 
within our club's budget.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.680
How much is in our budget?

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:19.680
Making that face won't get us more money!

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:23.860
It's because neither the astronomy club 
nor the geology club have any achievements.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:27.300
The clubs that are active, participating 
in tournaments and winning awards,

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:29.490
are the ones that get bigger budgets.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:32.740
It's true.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.950
So if we want to buy a great telescope...

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:39.410
Then do something to get results first.

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:41.430
I see.

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:43.840
So when are we having a barbecue?

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:44.720
Rejected!

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:45.790
Aw...

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:48.630
That reminds me. Where's Suzu?

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:51.080
Suzu-chan won't be joining the club.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.340
She's busy helping out at home.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:55.930
Oh, that's a shame.

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:58.220
If she had joined the geology club side,

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:01.540
our club would've been evenly 
balanced at three and three.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:02.810
Vice President...

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.470
Please cheer up!

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:07.320
I'll work hard enough for two people!

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:09.210
Thanks.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:12.780
Inose, your side-steps are super slow.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:16.700
<b>[Geology Club]
Mineral Observation
Fossil Collection
Cultural Festival</b>

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:16.700
<b>[Astronomy Club]
Observation Meetings
Photography
Cultural Festival</b>

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:16.700
I've listed our activities from 
before the merger for now.

00:16:17.020 --> 00:16:20.700
We already have the equipment, 
so I think we can keep doing most of these.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.860
The big problems are the 
ones that cost money:

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.540
our summer camps and the cultural festival.

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:27.400
Speaking of the cultural festival,

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:30.720
you aren't going to pull the same 
thing as last year, are you?

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:31.920
The same thing?

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:33.160
This?

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.630
You don't need to drag it out!

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:38.990
Going for sex appeal as a 
high schooler is shameful!

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.530
It was super popular, though.

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:45.740
Truth is, the vice president's been 
mad about that since last year.

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:47.220
Really?

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:49.440
Gathering customers
 through cosplay isn't fair!

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:53.700
You should have put together 
a proper exhibit, like us!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.240
<b>Geology
 Club</b>

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.240
<b>Examining the
 Rocks Near Us</b>

00:16:56.340 --> 00:17:00.450
Even though we only drew in about a tenth 
of the astronomy club's visitors.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.450
Inose, you're sharing too much.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.080
Ao, what's wrong?

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.920
We're kind of divided.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:16.130
You're right. There aren't activities 
that our groups would do together.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:18.700
I think we need some.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:20.900
A joint project, huh?

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:25.350
We could do our previous activities together, 
or come up with something new...

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:27.800
What do you think?

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.310
How did you understand her?

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:31.480
It's like you're telepathic.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:35.280
Um, I have a proposal.

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:39.510
Why don't we have our groups 
create a newsletter together?

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:40.760
A newsletter?

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:45.590
Yes. We'll print a sort of pamphlet 
introducing our club activities.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:46.800
That sounds fun!

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:47.370
Yeah.

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:50.170
What's the point of a newsletter, though?

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.380
Vice President, um...

00:17:53.090 --> 00:18:00.100
I know we didn't draw many visitors last year, 
but I thought we made a really good exhibit.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:56.880
<b>Look At Our Geological Map</b>

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:03.370
If we make our club more well-known,

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:06.920
I think lots more people will to come see us.

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:08.190
Inose...

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:12.400
Ino-senpai! Can we write whatever 
we want for the newsletter?

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:14.540
Ino-senpai?

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.490
Uh, sure. As long as it relates to our club.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:21.960
I could probably write an 
introduction to the planets.

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:24.200
If it has some interesting columns,

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.240
maybe more people will want to read it.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:28.960
Then I'll write...

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:32.460
a column introducing different minerals!

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:34.130
Sounds good.

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:36.050
What should we name our newsletter?

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:38.760
Yes! I have an idea!

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:44.390
<b>Weekly 
Find an 
Asteroid!</b>

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:41.140
<i>Weekly Find an Asteroid</i>!

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:44.390
We'll include telescope 
parts with each issue!

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:45.740
Rejected!

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:48.110
That's too focused on the astronomy side!

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:51.460
Weekly might be impossible, 
as well as including extras.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:54.230
What do you think would 
be good, Vice President?

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.650
<b>Mica Time 
Kirara Carat 
First Issue</b>

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.310
How's this?

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:58.650
No way!

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.440
I know! <i>Aim for an Asteroid</i>!

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:06.040
You girls have a lot of nerve.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:08.120
Senpai, calm down!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:09.320
It's going to be a challenge 
to get these two together.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:11.880
It needs to have both the 
astrology and geology club in it.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:11.880
That makes it worth the trouble.

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.520
This is hard.

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:17.920
Sorry to interrupt the fun, 
but it's time to leave school.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.380
Let's all go home.

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:21.570
Then... <i>Heaven & Earth</i>.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.890
That's not really...

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:23.680
Why not?

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:26.540
Something cuter would be better.

00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:28.160
Cuter...

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.240
They're not listening.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:32.440
Who wants a hamburger?

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:40.820
The stars are so pretty!

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:44.780
I do think something that conveys 
the charms of rocks would be best.

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:49.320
Vice President, let's just think about 
it while we eat some burgers!

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:50.450
Right.

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:52.460
Man, I'm hungry.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:57.880
<b>Sparkle</b>

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:57.880
<b>Earth Sciences 
Club Begins!</b>

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:56.730
<i>Sparkle</i>?

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.600
Makes sense.

00:19:59.600 --> 00:20:02.090
Both gems and stars do sparkle.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.700
It's not weird, is it?

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.970
No! It's really cute!

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:08.990
It's a great kirakira name!

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:10.560
Kirakira...

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:17.210
Sorry, Inose.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:20.980
I kept thinking about how to do a proper job,

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:25.940
but we need to get more people 
to understand what our club does.

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.410
Vice President...

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:32.680
We need to take down the 
barriers between ourselves first.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.170
Right!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:35.380
So, with that in mind...

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:38.190
How about this project?!

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:41.260
<b>Don't lose to
 the astronomy club!</b>

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:41.260
<b>Super Sexy 
Stones</b>

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:41.260
<i>That awkward side of you is so...</i>

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:43.010
Well?

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:45.480
Are you all getting along?

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:50.220
I was worried about Sakurai, since she's 
always prickly around unfamiliar people.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:54.920
Inose-chan's doing a good job 
mediating, so they're fine.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:55.860
I see.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:57.180
That's good.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:00.440
Oh, we have an addition to the budget.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:02.270
Here, take this.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:07.370
Tell everyone to make sure 
they're free next weekend.

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:10.830
You want to do this no matter what, huh?

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:16.620
The winter constellations are 
still pretty at this time of night.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.060
Yeah.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.340
<i>Hey, Ao?</i>

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:26.300
<i>It's so amazing that we're able to watch 
the stars and chat together like this.</i>

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:30.700
I'm really happy we're reunited.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:32.270
Ao?

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:34.730
Me, too.

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:40.040
I always hoped I might see you again.

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:42.460
Yeah.

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:46.590
<i>Well, see you at school tomorrow.</i>

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:47.950
Yeah.

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:53.860
<i>I want to find one.</i>

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:56.040
<i>I want to make it happen.</i>

00:21:57.810 --> 00:22:00.530
<i>Like we promised each other.</i>

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:44.530
02.
The Riverside Milky Way

00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:38.800
Next time, "The Riverside Milky Way."
